Preekstof — third-party components
==================================

What this app is built on, and under what terms. Two lists, because the difference matters:
what ships inside the repository travels with every copy, and what is fetched on first use
lands on the church's own computer and is never passed on by us.

The one to read carefully is YOLOv10n. It is AGPL-3.0, a licence that reaches into whatever
it is distributed with, and it is deliberately kept out of the repository for that reason.


SHIPPED IN THIS REPOSITORY
--------------------------

vision/face.onnx — YuNet face detection
    MIT. From huggingface.co/opencv/face_detection_yunet. Full text in vision/face.LICENSE.

templates/fonts/*.ttf — Anton, Barlow Condensed, Bebas Neue, Inter, Lora, Montserrat,
Nunito, Open Sans, Oswald, Poppins, Roboto
    SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each family's licence text sits next to the files as
    templates/fonts/OFL-<family>.txt.

selftest/proef.opus — the sentence the self-test speaks
    Not third-party and nobody's voice: made with espeak-ng, whose output is not a recording
    of a person. See selftest/README.md for the command that produced it.

frontend/public/icon.svg, the Preekstof name and mark
    Not third-party. Copyright Merijn Kersten, covered by LICENSE, and not granted for use
    apart from this software.


